<check_type:"Unix">

<if>
  <condition type:"AND">
    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "macOS 14 is installed"
      cmd         : "/usr/bin/sw_vers | /usr/bin/grep 'ProductVersion'"
      expect      : "^ProductVersion[\\s]*:[\\s]*@PLATFORM_VERSION@"
    </custom_item>
  </condition>

  <then>
    <report type:"PASSED">
      description : "CIS_Apple_macOS_14_Sonoma_STIG_v1.0.0_CAT_II.audit from CIS Apple macOS 14 Sonoma STIG v1.0.0"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      show_output : YES
    </report>

    <custom_item>
      type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
      description  : "1.1 APPL-14-000001"
      info         : "The macOS system must prevent Apple Watch from terminating a session lock.

GROUP ID: V-259418RULE ID: SV-259418r958400

Disabling Apple watches is a necessary step to ensuring that the information system retains a session lock until the user reestablishes access using authorized identification and authentication procedures."
      solution     : "Configure the macOS system to prevent Apple Watch from terminating a session lock by installing the \"com.apple.applicationaccess\" configuration profile."
      reference    : "800-171|3.1.10,800-171r3|03.01.10b.,800-53|AC-11b.,800-53r5|AC-11b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000056,CN-L3|8.1.4.1(b),GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(iii),ISO-27001-2022|A.7.7,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.11.2.8,ITSG-33|AC-11b.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|AM23e,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|8.1.8,PCI-DSSv4.0|8.2.8,Rule-ID|SV-259418r958400_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-000001,Vuln-ID|V-259418"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      expect       : "(?i)^(false|no|0)$"
      payload_key  : "allowAutoUnlock"
      payload_type : "com.apple.applicationaccess"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : BANNER_CHECK
      description : "1.10 APPL-14-000023"
      info        : "The macOS system must display the Standard Mandatory DOD Notice and Consent Banner at remote log on.

GROUP ID: V-259429RULE ID: SV-259429r958390

Displaying a standardized and approved use notification before granting access to the operating system ensures that users are provided with privacy and security notification verbiage that is consistent with applicable federal laws, Executive Orders, directives, policies, regulations, standards, and guidance.

System use notifications are required only for access via logon interfaces with human users and are not required when such human interfaces do not exist.

The banner must be formatted in accordance with DTM-08-060.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000023-GPOS-00006,SRG-OS-000024-GPOS-00007"
      solution    : "Configure the macOS system to display the Standard Mandatory DOD Notice and Consent Banner before granting remote access to the operating system by creating a text file containing the required DOD text.

Name the file \"banner\" and place it in \"/etc/\"."
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.9,800-171r3|03.01.09,800-53|AC-8a.,800-53|AC-8b.,800-53r5|AC-8a.,800-53r5|AC-8b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000048,CCI|CCI-000050,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.5,ITSG-33|AC-8a.,ITSG-33|AC-8b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|M5.2.5,NESA|T5.5.1,NIAv2|AM10a,NIAv2|AM10b,NIAv2|AM10c,NIAv2|AM10d,NIAv2|AM10e,NIAv2|AM10f,Rule-ID|SV-259429r958390_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-000023,TBA-FIISB|45.2.4,Vuln-ID|V-259429"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      file        : "/etc/banner"
      content     : "@BANNER_TEXT@"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
      description  : "1.100 APPL-14-002120"
      info         : "The macOS system must disable AppleID and Internet Account modifications.

GROUP ID: V-259520RULE ID: SV-259520r958478

The system must disable account modification.

Account modification includes adding additional or modifying internet accounts in Apple Mail, Calendar, Contacts, in the Internet Account System Setting Pane, or the AppleID System Setting Pane.

This prevents the addition of unauthorized accounts.

[IMPORTANT]

Some organizations may allow the use and configuration of the built-in Mail.app, Calendar.app, and Contacts.app for organizational communication. Information system security officers (ISSOs) may make the risk-based decision not to disable the Internet Accounts System Preference pane to avoid losing this functionality, but they are advised to first fully weigh the potential risks posed to their organization."
      solution     : "Configure the macOS system to disable account modification by installing the \"com.apple.applicationaccess\" configuration profile."
      reference    : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-259520r958478_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-002120,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-259520"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      expect       : "(?i)^(false|no|0)$"
      payload_key  : "allowAccountModification"
      payload_type : "com.apple.applicationaccess"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.101 APPL-14-002130"
      info        : "The macOS system must disable CD/DVD Sharing.

GROUP ID: V-259521RULE ID: SV-259521r958478

CD/DVD Sharing must be disabled."
      solution    : "Configure the macOS system to disable CD/DVD Sharing with the following command:

/bin/launchctl unload /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/com.apple.ODSAgent.plist"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-259521r958478_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-002130,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-259521"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      cmd         : "/usr/bin/pgrep -q ODSAgent; /bin/echo $?"
      expect      : "^1$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
      description  : "1.102 APPL-14-002140"
      info         : "The macOS system must disable content caching service.

GROUP ID: V-259522RULE ID: SV-259522r958478

Content caching must be disabled.

Content caching is a macOS service that helps reduce internet data usage and speed up software installation on Mac computers. It is not recommended for devices furnished to employees to act as a caching server."
      solution     : "Configure the macOS system to disable content caching service by installing the \"com.apple.applicationaccess\" configuration profile."
      reference    : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-259522r958478_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-002140,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-259522"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      expect       : "(?i)^(false|no|0)$"
      payload_key  : "allowContentCaching"
      payload_type : "com.apple.applicationaccess"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
      description  : "1.103 APPL-14-002150"
      info         : "The macOS system must disable iCloud desktop and document folder synchronization.

GROUP ID: V-259523RULE ID: SV-259523r958478

The macOS system's ability to automatically synchronize a user's desktop and documents folder to their iCloud Drive must be disabled.

Apple's iCloud service does not provide an organization with enough control over the storage and access of data and, therefore, automated file synchronization must be controlled by an organization approved service."
      solution     : "Configure the macOS system to disable iCloud desktop and document folder synchronization by installing the \"com.apple.applicationaccess\" configuration profile."
      reference    : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-259523r958478_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-002150,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-259523"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      expect       : "(?i)^(false|no|0)$"
      payload_key  : "allowCloudDesktopAndDocuments"
      payload_type : "com.apple.applicationaccess"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
      description  : "1.104 APPL-14-002160"
      info         : "The macOS system must disable iCloud Game Center.

GROUP ID: V-259524RULE ID: SV-259524r958478

This works only with supervised devices (MDM) and allows Apple Game Center to be disabled. The rationale is Game Center is using Apple ID and will share data on AppleID-based services; therefore, Game Center must be disabled. This setting also prohibits the functionality of adding friends to Game Center."
      solution     : "Configure the macOS system to disable iCloud Game Center by installing the \"com.apple.applicationaccess\" configuration profile."
      reference    : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-259524r958478_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-002160,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-259524"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      expect       : "(?i)^(false|no|0)$"
      payload_key  : "allowGameCenter"
      payload_type : "com.apple.applicationaccess"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
      description  : "1.105 APPL-14-002170"
      info         : "The macOS system must disable iCloud Private Relay.

GROUP ID: V-259525RULE ID: SV-259525r958478

Enterprise networks may be required to audit all network traffic by policy; therefore, iCloud Private Relay must be disabled.

Network administrators can also prevent the use of this feature by blocking DNS resolution of mask.icloud.com and mask-h2.icloud.com."
      solution     : "Configure the macOS system to disable the iCloud Private Relay by installing the \"com.apple.applicationaccess\" configuration profile."
      reference    : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-259525r958478_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-002170,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-259525"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      expect       : "(?i)^(false|no|0)$"
      payload_key  : "allowCloudPrivateRelay"
      payload_type : "com.apple.applicationaccess"
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
          description  : "DisableFMMiCloudSetting"
          expect       : "(?i)^(true|yes|[1-9][0-9]*)$"
          payload_key  : "DisableFMMiCloudSetting"
          payload_type : "com.apple.icloud.managed"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
          description  : "allowFindMyDevice"
          expect       : "(?i)^(false|no|0)$"
          payload_key  : "allowFindMyDevice"
          payload_type : "com.apple.applicationaccess"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
          description  : "allowFindMyFriends"
          expect       : "(?i)^(false|no|0)$"
          payload_key  : "allowFindMyFriends"
          payload_type : "com.apple.applicationaccess"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.106 APPL-14-002180"
          info        : "The macOS system must disable Find My service.

GROUP ID: V-259526RULE ID: SV-259526r958478

The Find My service must be disabled.

A Mobile Device Management (MDM) solution must be used to carry out remote locking and wiping instead of Apple's Find My service.

Apple's Find My service uses a personal AppleID for authentication. Organizations should rely on MDM solutions, which have much more secure authentication requirements, to perform remote lock and remote wipe."
          solution    : "Configure the macOS system to disable Find My service by installing the \"com.apple.applicationaccess\" configuration profile."
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-259526r958478_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-002180,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-259526"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>
    </if>

    <custom_item>
      type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
      description  : "1.107 APPL-14-002190"
      info         : "The macOS system must disable password autofill.

GROUP ID: V-259527RULE ID: SV-259527r958478

Password Autofill must be disabled.

macOS allows users to save passwords and use the Password Autofill feature in Safari and compatible apps. To protect against malicious users gaining access to the system, this feature must be disabled to prevent users from being prompted to save passwords in applications."
      solution     : "Configure the macOS system to disable password autofill by installing the \"com.apple.applicationaccess\" configuration profile."
      reference    : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-259527r958478_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-002190,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-259527"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      expect       : "(?i)^(false|no|0)$"
      payload_key  : "allowPasswordAutoFill"
      payload_type : "com.apple.applicationaccess"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
      description  : "1.108 APPL-14-002200"
      info         : "The macOS system must disable personalized advertising.

GROUP ID: V-259528RULE ID: SV-259528r958478

Ad tracking and targeted ads must be disabled.

