    <custom_item>
      type         : MACOSX_OSASCRIPT
      description  : "1.15 APPL-14-000033"
      info         : "The macOS system must disable FileVault automatic log on.

GROUP ID: V-259434RULE ID: SV-259434r958472

If FileVault is enabled, automatic log on must be disabled, so that both FileVault and login window authentication are required.

The default behavior of macOS when FileVault is enabled is to automatically log on to the computer once successfully passing user's FileVault credentials.

Note: DisableFDEAutoLogin does not have to be set on Apple Silicon-based macOS systems that are smartcard enforced, as smartcards are available at preboot."
      solution     : "Configure the macOS system to disable filevault automatic login by installing the \"com.apple.loginwindow\" configuration profile.

Note: To ensure continued access to the operating system, consult the supplemental guidance provided with the STIG before applying the configuration profile."
      reference    : "800-171|3.1.1,800-171r3|03.01.02,800-53|AC-3,800-53r5|AC-3,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000213,CN-L3|8.1.4.2(f),CN-L3|8.1.4.11(b),CN-L3|8.1.10.2(c),CN-L3|8.5.3.1,CN-L3|8.5.4.1(a),CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.3,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.20,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.5,ITSG-33|AC-3,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T4.2.1,NESA|T5.4.4,NESA|T5.4.5,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.2,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM3,NIAv2|SS29,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-259434r958472_rule,STIG-ID|APPL-14-000033,TBA-FIISB|31.1,Vuln-ID|V-259434"
      see_also     : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      expect       : "(?i)^(true|yes|[1-9][0-9]*)$"
