      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/24070"
      cmd         : "/usr/bin/awk -F':' '/^policy/ {print $NF}' /etc/security/audit_control | /usr/bin/tr ',' '\\n' | /usr/bin/grep -Ec 'ahlt'"
      expect      : "^1$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.36 APPL-14-001012"
      info        : "The macOS system must configure audit log files to be owned by root.

GROUP ID: V-259456RULE ID: SV-259456r958434

Audit log files must be owned by root.

The audit service must be configured to create log files with the correct ownership to prevent normal users from reading audit logs.

